      "text": "Outcome: resolve_altitude. Tariq, this operation is not ready for release because the maximum planned altitude is 500 ft AGL. That exceeds the Part 107 limit of 400 ft AGL. The evidence shows no structure-proximity exception, so the flight plan altitude must be lowered or justified before release.\n\nThe other checks pass on the evidence provided:\n- **Pilot:** Mei Mensah holds a valid remote pilot certificate and has current aeronautical knowledge.\n- **Airspace:** The location is uncontrolled Class G airspace, so no controlled-airspace authorization is needed.\n- **Visibility:** Forecast visibility is 5 statute miles, above the 3-mile minimum.\n- **Cloud clearance:** Planned separation meets the 500 ft below / 2,000 ft horizontal minimums.\n- **Speed:** Maximum planned groundspeed is 80 mph, within the 100 mph limit.\n\nAltitude is the only blocking item.",
